{"data": [{"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:15:20.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2114828245723971870"], "id": "2114828245723971870", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "nytimes.com/2026/10/26/wor…", "end": 854, "expanded_url": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/26/world/asia/china-communist-party-xi-forever-purge.html", "start": 831, "url": "https://t.co/uYJwtMBJoM"}]}, "text": "\"Xi’s suspicions may extend even higher, perhaps to Wang Qishan, 78, the former leader of the Central Commission for Discipline Inspection. Mr. Wang oversaw Mr. Xi’s anticorruption campaign in its 1st phase & is now retired.\n\nSeveral of Wang’s longtime aides—including Zhou Liang, a financial official, & Li Xiaohong, a disciplinary official—have been detained on suspicion of corruption. \n\nDong Hong, another former secretary of Wang, was imprisoned on corruption charges in 2022.\n\nThis yr, 2 of Wang’s former subordinates were demoted from the Central Commission for Discipline Inspection, suggesting they too might be under a cloud.\n\nWang himself has not been accused of wrongdoing...but the cases have prompted speculation that Xi is wary of the influence that retired officials could retain through their networks & protégés\"\nhttps://t.co/uYJwtMBJoM"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 845, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "repost_count": 0}, "text": "\"Xi’s suspicions may extend even higher, perhaps to Wang Qishan, 78, the former leader of the Central Commission for Discipline Inspection. Mr. Wang oversaw Mr. Xi’s anticorruption campaign in its 1st phase &amp; is now retired.\n\nSeveral of Wang’s longtime aides—including Zhou Liang,", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2114828245723971870"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114837731868094464"]}, "author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:53:02.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2114837735357743203"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "To invade red blood cells, the deadly protists create temporary molecular portals that disappear behind them — doors we can now see in fine detail.", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/malaria-parasi…", "end": 218, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/malaria-parasite-caught-in-the-act-of-breaking-and-entering-20261023/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113645763972481024/y5u7T7ny?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113645763972481024/y5u7T7ny?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 195, "status": 200, "title": "Malaria Parasite Caught in the Act of Breaking and Entering | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/malaria-parasite-caught-in-the-act-of-breaking-and-entering-20261023/", "url": "https://t.co/JyPSUT29CU"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/wBt8lJ4Ukv", "end": 242, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2114837735357743203/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114837731868094464", "start": 219, "url": "https://t.co/wBt8lJ4Ukv"}]}, "id": "2114837735357743203", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 761, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "repost_count": 1}, "text": "Chi-Min Ho and her team were able to image the exact moment malaria invades a red blood cell, in unprecedented detail. This knowledge could help inform the next generation of malaria treatments. https://t.co/JyPSUT29CU https://t.co/wBt8lJ4Ukv", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2114837735357743203"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2114836981934960641"]}, "author_id": "15134240", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:50:08.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2114837004718362783"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/XK2CYU5cwD", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/NIH/status/2114837004718362783/video/1", "media_key": "13_2114836981934960641", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/XK2CYU5cwD"}]}, "id": "2114837004718362783", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "nih.gov/som", "end": 373, "expanded_url": "https://www.nih.gov/som", "start": 350, "url": "https://t.co/cGSSpWpSpa"}]}, "text": "Tiny models. Big research potential.\n\nOrganoids are small, lab-grown models that mimic how human organs work, helping scientists better understand disease and explore new treatments. Learn how the NIH Standardized Organoid Modeling (SOM) Center is working to make these powerful research tools more reliable and accessible. \n\nExplore the SOM Center: https://t.co/cGSSpWpSpa."}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 942, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "repost_count": 0}, "text": "Tiny models. Big research potential.\n\nOrganoids are small, lab-grown models that mimic how human organs work, helping scientists better understand disease and explore new treatments. Learn how the NIH Standardized Organoid Modeling (SOM) Center is working to make these powerful https://t.co/XK2CYU5cwD", "url": "https://x.com/NIH/status/2114837004718362783"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114832993038811136"]}, "author_id": "86626845", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:35:41.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2114833368298950809"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 62, "id": "120206023", "start": 51, "username": "AnnalsofIM"}, {"end": 100, "id": "3094610676", "start": 84, "username": "pranavrajpurkar"}], "urls": [{"description": "Health care has come to rely on “human in the loop” postdeployment monitoring of artificial intelligence applications to ensure patient safety. However, the authors argue that “human in the loop” p...", "display_url": "acpjournals.org/doi/10.7326/AN…", "end": 160, "expanded_url": "https://www.acpjournals.org/doi/10.7326/ANNALS-26-02753", "images": [{"height": 322, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114833372250017792/T6EzHD3h?format=png&name=orig", "width": 242}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114833372250017792/T6EzHD3h?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 137, "status": 200, "title": "The Illusion of Oversight in Clinical Artificial Intelligence: Human Out of the Loop? | Annals of Internal Medicine", "unwound_url": "https://www.acpjournals.org/doi/10.7326/ANNALS-26-02753", "url": "https://t.co/n1gOaQld1R"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/s0jOP3Ylmo", "end": 184, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2114833368298950809/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114832993038811136", "start": 161, "url": "https://t.co/s0jOP3Ylmo"}]}, "id": "2114833368298950809", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 4380, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "repost_count": 2}, "text": "What about humans-in-the loop with medical AI?\nOur @AnnalsofIM paper just published\n@pranavrajpurkar, Christine Zhou, Alexandra Willauer\nhttps://t.co/n1gOaQld1R https://t.co/s0jOP3Ylmo", "url": "https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2114833368298950809"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114833200430063616"]}, "author_id": "32372834", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:35:02.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2114833204884455907"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 31, "id": "2326120952", "start": 15, "username": "ScienceAdvances"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/CsjCzZl7MA", "end": 284, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2114833204884455907/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114833200430063616", "start": 261, "url": "https://t.co/CsjCzZl7MA"}]}, "id": "2114833204884455907", "note_tweet": {"entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 31, "id": "2326120952", "start": 15, "username": "ScienceAdvances"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "scim.ag/4yyM9UE", "end": 284, "expanded_url": "https://scim.ag/4yyM9UE", "start": 261, "url": "https://t.co/RBJetYXiN8"}]}, "text": "Researchers in @ScienceAdvances have developed a multiplexed and implantable fiber sensor that monitors the bloodstream for real-time levels of sodium and potassium, two electrolytes that regulate important bodily functions like heart rhythm and fluid balance. https://t.co/RBJetYXiN8"}, "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 3707, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "repost_count": 1}, "text": "Researchers in @ScienceAdvances have developed a multiplexed and implantable fiber sensor that monitors the bloodstream for real-time levels of sodium and potassium, two electrolytes that regulate important bodily functions like heart rhythm and fluid balance. https://t.co/CsjCzZl7MA", "url": "https://x.com/ScienceMagazine/status/2114833204884455907"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:29:43.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2114831867622957276"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The Trump administration removed several security, privacy and transparency requirements for vendors of EHR software.", "display_url": "trib.al/3PJ4AiN", "end": 141, "expanded_url": "https://trib.al/3PJ4AiN", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114831874526736384/AjwqtLig?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114831874526736384/AjwqtLig?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 118, "status": 200, "title": "HHS relaxes security, transparency rules for health record software used by hospitals", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/10/26/health-data-interoperability-hti5-relaxes-privacy-security-requirements/?utm_campaign=twitter_organic&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social", "url": "https://t.co/zr2DXR9xlG"}]}, "id": "2114831867622957276", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 650, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "repost_count": 0}, "text": "The Trump administration removed several security, privacy and transparency requirements for vendors of EHR software. https://t.co/zr2DXR9xlG", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2114831867622957276"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114826137755103232"]}, "author_id": "86626845", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:10:01.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2114826911058890937"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 231, "id": "120206023", "start": 220, "username": "AnnalsofIM"}], "urls": [{"description": "Background: Obesity and early-onset cancer are both increasing among young adults, yet evidence remains limited. Objective: To assess associations between obesity and early-onset cancer risk in young adults. Design: Nationwide population-based cohort study. Setting: Korean National Health Insurance Service database, 2009 to 2021. Patients: 6 313 338 adults aged 20 to 39 years without prior cancer, from a national health screening program. Measurements: Body mass index (BMI) was categorized into 5 groups (underweight to class II obesity) according to Asian-specific criteria. The outcome was incident cancer. Results: During a mean follow-up of 11.2 years, 151 893 cancer cases occurred. Ten-year cumulative incidence ranged from 1.84% (95% CI, 1.83% to 1.86%) in the normal-weight group to 2.24% (CI, 2.22% to 2.27%) in class I obesity and 2.62% (CI, 2.56% to 2.68%) in class II obesity, with absolute risk differences of 0.40% (CI, 0.39% to 0.41%) and 0.78% (CI, 0.73% to 0.82%). The relative ", "display_url": "acpjournals.org/doi/full/10.73…", "end": 219, "expanded_url": "https://www.acpjournals.org/doi/full/10.7326/ANNALS-25-02612", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114826922203168769/vKeh_Tm8?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 960}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114826922203168769/vKeh_Tm8?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 196, "status": 200, "title": "Obesity and Cancer Risk in Young Adults in Korea: A Nationwide Health Screening Cohort Study: Annals of Internal Medicine: Vol 0, No 0", "unwound_url": "https://www.acpjournals.org/doi/abs/10.7326/ANNALS-25-02612?journalCode=aim", "url": "https://t.co/XC8hevDJFb"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/lNnqQDKBZZ", "end": 255, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2114826911058890937/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114826137755103232", "start": 232, "url": "https://t.co/lNnqQDKBZZ"}]}, "id": "2114826911058890937", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 21, "impression_count": 7720, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 8, "repost_count": 8}, "text": "The link between obesity and early-onset cancer.\nA nationwide study of 6.3 million people, age 20-39,  with no prior cancer, by BMI and waist circumference, with 11 year follow-up, in South Korea\nhttps://t.co/XC8hevDJFb @AnnalsofIM https://t.co/lNnqQDKBZZ", "url": "https://x.com/EricTopol/status/2114826911058890937"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2114837818380107776"]}, "author_id": "487118986", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:53:22.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2114837820972184030"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "xhtxs.cn/bfYr", "end": 142, "expanded_url": "https://xhtxs.cn/bfYr", "start": 119, "unwound_url": "https://english.news.cn/20261027/63d44aec45c544ab9be3732bde82fba5/c.html", "url": "https://t.co/FR1hvYpI4y"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/rwGfT9oQu9", "end": 166, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/XHNews/status/2114837820972184030/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2114837818380107776", "start": 143, "url": "https://t.co/rwGfT9oQu9"}]}, "id": "2114837820972184030", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1452, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "repost_count": 1}, "text": "Jordan launches airstrikes on southern Syria, says the operation hit militants behind a deadly church attack in Jordan https://t.co/FR1hvYpI4y https://t.co/rwGfT9oQu9", "url": "https://x.com/XHNews/status/2114837820972184030"}, {"author_id": "23922797", "created_at": "2026-10-26T21:51:20.000Z", "edit_history_post_ids": ["2114837306829889883"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Regional tensions in the Middle East have risen ahead of Israel’s pivotal elections on 